# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Elizabeth Stippell et al. (2023). Building a DFT+U machine learning interatomic potential for uranium dioxide.
#   Artificial Intelligence Chemistry. doi:10.1016/j.aichem.2023.100042
#
# Version read: submittedVersion (sha256 cb6dcaa17c2d0669...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 359 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/stippell2023.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the active-learning DFT (PBE) data set of 96-atom UO2
# cells (query-by-committee over eight ANI models, MLIP-MD from about
# 6,500 classical-FF seed configurations; about 25k configurations after
# removing about 400 metastable outliers), the reduced DFT+U data set
# (about 2,000 configurations, U-J ramped to 3.99 eV), the eight-member
# ANI ensemble trained on DFT (MLIP-DFT) and its transfer-learned DFT+U
# version with layers 0 and 3 frozen (MLIP-DFT+U, TL(0,3)), with the
# test RMSEs stated in the text. Thermophysical properties and defect
# energies are properties.

